report={'status':'BOUNDED_OFFLINE_TIMING_REVIEW_COMPLETE','utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'hardware_or_network_access':False,'production_parameters_changed':False,'frozen_payload_manifest_sha256':sha(LC/'payload_manifest.json'),'all265_payload_bindings_still_match':True,
 'main_finding':'Unchanged kernel/diagnostic ISO can pass through the custom EFI loader when TCG is explicitly single-threaded, even without icount or an explicit RTC override. Existing default-TCG paths reached a concrete early timer self-test failure. This supports a virtual execution/timer-delivery interaction, not an established malformed boot_params defect. A specific QEMU scheduling defect is not proven.',
 'exact_kernel_static_evidence':{'kernel_sha256':timing['kernel_sha256'],'vmlinux_sha256':timing['vmlinux_sha256'],'gzip_offset':timing['gzip_offset'],'configuration':'CONFIG_HZ_1000=y, CONFIG_X86_TSC=y, CONFIG_HPET_TIMER=y','timer_function':'timer_irq_works at staticVA0xffffffff8330aff0','jiffies_initial_read':'0xffffffff8330b017 instruction488b1da2c98fff reads jiffies_64 intoRBX','irq_enable':'0xffffffff8330b048 bytesff15b2c593ff; initial function pointer resolves to pv_native_irq_enable (runtime patching not traced)','tsc_loop':['0xffffffff8330b075 RDTSC records initial counter','0xffffffff8330b09b RDTSC; subtract initial counter at0xffffffff8330b0a4','0xffffffff8330b0a7 bytes4881faff596202 compares delta with39999999 (0x26259ff); exceeding it leaves wait','Loop also exits when current jiffies is later than sampled_jiffies+4'],
 'final_condition':'0xffffffff8330b190..0xffffffff8330b19e reads jiffies_64 again and returns1 only if final_jiffies > initial_jiffies+4. Thus at least5 ticks must arrive before the bounded self-test ends, independent of seeing valid boot files.',
 'panic_binding':'setup_IO_APIC staticVA0xffffffff8330be60 calls panic at0xffffffff8330ca5e. Its return address0xffffffff8330ca63 is setup_IO_APIC+0xc03, exactly matching the observed panic backtrace. The preceding branch follows a failed timer_irq_works call at0xffffffff8330ca04.','meaning':'The bytes establish the timer-progress requirement. They do not expose the actual TSC/jiffies values at the failed instant because those were not dynamically traced. There is also a non-TSC fallback delay path.'},
 'observed_existing_runs':cases,'independent_controls':controls['controls'],
 'handoff_source_review':{'observation':'bootstrap.c uses firmware LoadImage and StartImage on the pinned PE kernel. It sets only LoadedImage LoadOptions/LoadOptionsSize for the child and offers the fixed initrd using LoadFile2; it does not build a Linux boot_params block or directly program PIT/IO-APIC.','kernel_source':'x86-stub.c:534..581 efi_pe_entry allocates and zeroes PARAM_SIZE, sets root_flags1,vid_modeffff,type_of_loader21,initrd_addr_maxINT_MAX and converts LoadedImage cmdline; efi_stub_entry then loads initrd, populates EFI/E820/graphics and exits boot services.','diagnostic':'A separate prior debug loader reported TPL_APPLICATION4 and RFLAGS0202 before kernel start; IF was set at that point. That snapshot does not prove interrupt delivery throughout later kernel initialization.','limit':'Direct fw_cfg and PE boot flows are not identical; exact OVMF fw_cfg-created boot_params and runtime IRQ state were not captured. No evidence here justifies changing kernel boot parameter layout or bypassing its timer check.'},
 'qemu_primary_documentation':{'local':'Bundled QEMU11.1 docs, devel/tcg-icount.html and system/invocation.html','observations':['icount bases virtual time on executed guest instructions and schedules execution budgets around timer deadlines.','Instruction counting is incompatible with multi-threaded TCG and is not cycle-accurate hardware simulation.','Explicit RTCclock=vm is recommended for deterministic icount use; the independent default-RTC icount control still booted.'],
 'inference':'Changing threading and virtual-time coordination can change whether at least5 timer ticks are delivered before the kernel TSC-bound check completes. The exact previous default threading implementation and failed counter values were not instrumented.'},
 'decisions':['Keep the frozen kernel/initramfs/production commandline unchanged; no noapic,notsc,timer-check bypass or IRQ hook was added.','The independently successful explicit-single/no-icount control prevents attributing recovery solely to icount or RTCclock=vm.','Use uefi_lab final frozen ISO and its own SATA/USB/repeated tests as final loader evidence. This assist used an earlier unchanged serial-debug ISO with old597B refusal payload solely for timing comparison.','No additional random variants are needed for this bounded review. If stronger root-cause attribution is needed later, instrument TSC/jiffies and IRQdelivery at the exact check, keeping kernel bytes unchanged in localVM only.'],
 'limitations':['Only one run per independent control; results do not establish deterministic behavior under all host scheduling loads.','QEMU timing profiles are test environments, not ASUS hardware characteristics.','A PID1 DMI refusal is a boot-path observation, not physical USB capacity acceptance or a flash/deployment approval.'],
 'inputs':[{'path':str(p.relative_to(ROOT)),'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':sha(p)} for p in inputs]}
